   "id": "ai-capex-selloff",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Alphabet's cash burn sets off a tech sell-off on Wall Street",
   "when": "Thu 29 – Fri 30 Oct · US session",
   "what": "Alphabet fell about 13% on Thursday, its worst day since its 2004 listing. It reported negative free cash flow of $9.07 billion against about $2.7 billion expected. Search growth also missed forecasts, and 2026 capex stays at $195-205 billion. Microsoft held roughly flat after spending less than forecast. On Friday the S&P 500 closed down 1.82% at 7,580 and the Nasdaq down 2.86%.",
   "why": "Investors are asking whether AI spending will pay off. Your US funds are mostly large tech companies, so a fall like this lands there first. Those funds are priced at their 29 Oct NAVs this morning, before Friday's fall. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30.",
